course: dictionary
lesson: 13069
title: Fermentation: tiny things at work
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Fermentation is a natural change caused by tiny living things, such as yeast or bacteria. They break down sugars in food, and this often makes gas, acid or alcohol.
explain: You can see fermentation in a science test. Mix yeast with sugar and warm water in a bottle, and fit a balloon over the top. «During fermentation, the yeast made gas, and the balloon blew up.» The gas is what fills the balloon.
explain: Fermentation is also how bread rises, and how yoghurt, cheese, sauerkraut and kimchi are made. Foods made this way are called «fermented foods». Wine and beer are made by fermentation too.
explain: The word can also be used in a more formal way for excitement or unrest among people. «There was fermentation in the town after the news.» Here the word does not mean food at all, so always check the sentence around it.
fact: Fermentation is a natural change in which tiny living things break down sugars.
fact: «Fermentation» is a noun. The verb is «ferment» and the adjective is «fermented».
fact: Yeast is a tiny living thing that makes gas during fermentation, which is why bread rises.
fact: «Fermented foods» include yoghurt, cheese, sauerkraut, kimchi, wine and beer.
fact: Fermentation can also mean excitement or unrest among people. This is a more formal use of the word.
exercise: «During fermentation, the yeast made bubbles of gas.» What is fermentation? | A way of freezing food | *A natural change where tiny living things break down sugars | A type of sharp knife | A kind of metal used in cooking
exercise: Which food is made using fermentation? | *Yoghurt | Ice cubes | A glass of water | A slice of plain apple
exercise: In the balloon experiment, what makes the balloon blow up? | Cold air from the fridge | Sugar melting in the bottle | Sound from the bottle | *Gas made by the yeast
test: Which living things cause fermentation in bread? | Rocks and sand | Large fish in a river | *Tiny living things like yeast | Metal baking pans
test: In «There was fermentation in the town after the news», what does fermentation mean? | Cold weather | *Excitement or unrest among people | Making cheese | Gas in a balloon
exam: What does the yeast do during fermentation that makes bread rise? | Turns the dough into ice | Freezes the dough | Cools the dough | *Makes gas
